name mig29-rwr-blind-1
timeout 240

# "USING YOUR RADAR BLINDS YOUR RWR FORWARD" — the single most tactically consequential line in
# doc/modules/mig29/defence-rwr-cm.md (§2.7 item 11): the SPO-15 is an analogue receiver that cannot
# filter the HPRF of the aircraft it is installed in, so WHILE THE OWN FCR RADIATES THE WHOLE FORWARD
# HEMISPHERE OF THE DEVICE IS DISABLED. On this jet the act of looking costs you the warning that would
# have told you to stop looking.
#
# The run makes that one switch the only variable:
#
#   viper    flies straight and level with the APG-68 in CRM, radiating, dead ahead of the MiG. It never
#            changes anything. Its `fcr_on` column is the control: the beam is on the whole time.
#   fulcrum  flies at it with the SPO-15 on and the N019 on the power-up EMISSION OFF position. It
#            therefore HEARS the Viper from the first sweep -- rwr_threats = 1, bearing quantised to
#            a channel centre (the SPO-15 reports the channel that fired, not an angle it never
#            measured), and the threat sits in the forward channels.
#
#   AT t = 40 s A GCI CALL COMES IN. It is briefed as mission data, and the pilot has to TYPE it: three
#   entries, one per decision tick, in the DED latency class -- antenna elevation from the range-angle
#   method, the ZONE switch, and then ILLUM. The third entry is what turns the radar on, and at that
#   moment the SPO-15's forward hemisphere goes dark while the Viper is still radiating exactly as
#   before. Nothing about the emitter changed. Nothing about the geometry changed.
#
# WHAT TO READ, from events.log and the two telemetry files:
#   gci BRAA / ENTER_ELEV / ENTER_ZONE / RADAR_ILLUM   -- the entry chain and how many seconds it took
#   spo15 FORWARD_BLANK on=1                           -- the blanking, with its half-angle
#   rwr THREAT_BLIND                                   -- the warning going inaudible, and
#   rwr_threats (fulcrum)  1 -> 0                      -- one hold time (2 s) later
#   fcr_on (viper)         1 throughout                -- the control: the emitter never stopped
#   fcr_on (fulcrum)       0 -> 1                      -- the cause, in the same trace
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the verdict AND the pass. This is a measurement rig; neither
# aircraft has anything to complete. exit 2 (CRASH) would be a failure -- both legs are level at
# 8 000 m.

unit viper
  module f16
  team hostile
  spawn 46.90000 7.30000 8000 270.0 400        # ~35 nm east of the MiG, head-on, radiating
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode crm                             # the power-up search: +-60 deg, radiating throughout
  set rwr off                                  # this jet is the emitter; its own receiver is not the subject
  wp 46.90000 6.40000 8000 400                 # one long level leg west

unit fulcrum
  module mig29
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 6.60000 8000 90.0 400         # level east, straight at it
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set rwr on                                   # the SPO-15: 360 deg azimuth, +-30 deg elevation
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission off                        # the power-up position: this jet starts SILENT, by doctrine
  set brief_gci 40 090 60 8                    # the controller, at t=40 s: bearing 090, 60 km, 8 km
  wp 46.90000 7.40000 8000 400
